        "text": "The theoretical foundation of formative assessment is rooted in constructivist learning theory, which emphasizes the importance of active student engagement and knowledge construction through interaction with the learning environment (Piaget, 1950). In the context of formative assessment, this theory suggests that feedback should be a continuous, interactive process that supports students in actively constructing their understanding of mathematical concepts. Furthermore, formative assessment aligns with Vygotsky's (1978) Zone of Proximal Development, which posits that students can achieve higher levels of understanding with appropriate scaffolding from teachers and peers. In this regard, formative assessment provides the necessary scaffolding to guide students through their learning challenges.",
