        "text": "The formative evaluation fulfills a predominantly pedagogical purpose of continuous regulation-self-regulation of the activity. Achieving this goal implies, on the one hand, the observance of the qualities of the formative evaluation which has an analytical, continuous, diagnostic, corrective character. On the other hand, the capitalization of these qualities typical to the formative evaluation creates premises for the optimization of the final evaluation. \n\nSummative evaluation fulfills a social function, of certifying the results at the end of an activity/activities. This veiling strategy involves several operations: \n\n•the appreciation of the acquisitions at the level of criterion evaluation in relation to the achieved performance objectives, which allows the student's self-evaluation, and normative in relation to the general norms, which determines the students' hierarchy; \n\n•grading the products in relation to the established objectives, by applying standardized tests; \n\n•certification of competencies that express the sum or product of knowledge (savoir), strategies (savoir-faire), attitudes (savoir-être) and the final expression of school success / failure in relation to which a compensatory pedagogy can be proposed. \n\nThe share of the three types of regulation depends on the specifics of each evaluation strategy. The combined use of the three strategies gives the assessment complexity by engaging and structuring acquisitions through specific techniques of adjustment, integration and appreciation of the new behavior.",
