        "text": "The text, practice test, and final SA comprehension assessment were the same as in Experiment 2. For each of the two practice test formats three versions were created, one with knowledge of correct response (KCR) feedback that indicated whether a student's answer was correct or not along with the correct answer, and another with elaborative feedback (EF), which was identical to KCR but in addition to stating the correct answer also provided an explanation why that answer was correct using sentences copied from the text (see Tables 4 and 5). \n\nFor each of the five multiple-choice questions, feedback was displayed on a separate page. Because true-false items were created to match the four multiple-choice response options, for the purposes of feedback equivalency across conditions, the true-false items were clustered in these groups of four. The explanations included as part of EF were identical across multiple-choice and true-false conditions. To ensure that participants would have to engage with the feedback at least on some level, they were required to click on the correct response for each question before being able to advance to the next page. For both practice testing conditions there also was a no-feedback control condition (NF).",
