      "snippet": {
        "text": "In the study we ask the following research questions: RQ1: How can comprehensive multi-approach formative assessment be enacted in classroom practice? RQ2: Which characteristics of classroom practices, argued to influence student motivational characteristics that affect behavioural engagement and autonomous motivation, can be identified in the studied formative assessment practice? RQ3: Does behavioural engagement increase and motivation become more autonomous in students in the intervention class, and how do changes in engagement and type of motivation in the intervention class compare with changes in the two control classes? \n\nSince the present study is a case study involving only one class, the aim of the investigation of changes in engagement and type of motivation (Research question 3), over time and in comparison with two control classes, is not to produce results that can be generalised to other populations and contexts. The aim is mainly to provide a backdrop against which the results to Research question 2 may be interpreted.",
