      "snippet": {
        "text": "Formative assessment is an effective, student-centered learning strategy designed to provide relevant and ongoing feedback (Black & Wiliam, 1998;Hasanah et al., 2021). This strategy not only helps students understand the material in depth, but also encourages the application of their knowledge in real situations to improve critical thinking, collaboration, and communication skills (Nikolaevna Shapovalova & Efremova, 2020;Sadler, 1989). Through formative assessment, students are encouraged to reflect on their learning outcomes, discuss, and receive feedback that helps them improve their performance continuously. This approach is also able to increase student motivation and engagement in learning, because students can see the relevance of the learning process to their real needs. In this study, an in-depth analysis of 30 articles that met the eligibility criteria showed that formative assessment has an important role in improving learning outcomes. \n\nThe results of the analysis of 30 articles show a formative-summative evaluation model on mathematics learning outcomes through differentiated learning in high school students. This study shows that the formative-summative evaluation model significantly affects mathematics learning outcomes in high school students through differentiated learning (Gaspersz & Suranto, 2023). Formative assessment (FA) significantly improves learning outcomes by promoting student engagement and fostering a learning community. It allows for ongoing feedback, which helps students identify their strengths and weaknesses, thereby improving their skills and understanding. This study shows that effective online FA can create a student-centered focus, leading to meaningful learning experiences. Although there was no significant difference in self-regulation skills, FA practices positively influenced students' attitudes toward learning, highlighting its effectiveness in educational settings (Sanchez-Lopez et al., 2023). The Online 